PART 4 - 

1. Unsupervised or Supervised learning - This problem is best solved using supervised learning. It relies on previous 
data and already has a defined label that the model is trying to determine. Trying to determine fraud based on random variables
would result in many false positives or negatives that would make it extremely hard for customers to use accounts, as they would 
constantly be getting flagged or losing money to fraud. Therefore, supervised learning will give the best possible data so the model can 
make accurate predictions. 

2. Classification or Prediction - This model is clearly based on a classification label. It is determining a yes/no option with
whether or not the transactions occurring on the customer’s account are fraud. A prediction would make no sense because the model does not 
care about the actual amount, it only wants to see if there is fraud. It does look at the variance from the median spending, but ultimately 
only the difference matters, not the actual amount, so classification is much better. 


PART 5 - 

1. Three possible data quality problems - One data quality problem could be the 'ratio to median purchase price'. Outliers in the customers data
for that variable could mean incorrect assumptions are made by the model. Another issue would be customers that have moved home addresses 
so the 'distance from home' variable is outdated and showing an extremely high value. Finally, in some cases, the distance from last transaction
is very high, but online order is also true, meaning it likely should not be marked fraud just based on those, but it was by the AI.

2. What would happen if the data quality was poor - With poor data, the model will be fed unreliable results in its supervised learning. Due to
this, it will have trouble accurately predicting if fraud is occurring. The bank might either get a lot of false reports or no reports at all 
of fraud and will lose customers and possibly even get sued or shut down because of how important this issue is. With safety as one of its number
one priority to stay in business, poor data quality for fraud detection would be extremely devastating. 


