Business Problem: A bank wants to detect any and all fraud occurring in customer accounts

Data Needed: Normal transaction prices, distance of transaction from usual locations, and whether or not the 
customer has shopped there already are essential data points

Learning Type: Supervised learning 
Why: You need to see previous occurrences to know what signs to look for when fraud is happening 

Classification or Prediction: Classification - (Fraud / Not Fraud) 

Data Quality Problems: Outliers in normal transaction price, moving home addresses, distance not calculating for being an online purchase

Business Benefit: They attract more customers by promoting a safer environment for their money 

Potential Risk: The model predicts many false positives and people are frustrated at not being able to easily access their money
















